Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:41:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07985/11362] [outer-loop] MAX_ACTIONS budget sweep on the
 scored path: (budget -> wins, TIME)

400 actions/game is SELF-IMPOSED (CarnotAgent.MAX_ACTIONS, arc_competition_agent.py:6230
-- a documented override point; the framework's own Playback subclass sets 1e6). This
measures what raising it actually buys, and what it costs. NOTHING WAS CHANGED: the sweep
varies arc_leaderboard_eval.run_game(budget=N), never the shipped default.

400 cells: 25 public games x 3 seeds x {200,400,1000,2000,4000} per-seed matched (375),
plus a 1-seed {..,8000} extension reported as a SEPARATE design (25). E3AgentPolicy,
shipped flags (all EIGHT pinned per cell), LLM-off.

WINS (median over 3 seeds, per-seed matched -- the any-seed union is recorded as a
labelled diagnostic only):
  b200 2 | b400 4 | b1000 9 | b2000 11 | b4000 12   (1-seed extension: b8000 12, saturated)
Every step favours the higher budget with ZERO regressions; two-sided sign tests on
matched cells: 0.0625 / 6.1e-5 / 0.0156 / 0.25.

TIME IS NOT THE CONSTRAINT. 25-game wall 144s -> 840s. At the TIGHTEST envelope (110
games / 8h) budget 4000 costs 11.3% of the usable loop wall; the analytic crossing sits
at ~47,000 actions/game. The binding bound is instead the documented-but-UNCONFIRMED
gateway step rate (10/s x 8h = ~288k steps = 2,618 actions/game at 110 games).

THE FINDING THAT SHOULD GOVERN THE DECISION. Wins are not the scored quantity. The score
is a sum of per-level min(human/agent,1)^2 terms and the post-solve tail-cutter is
DISABLED (SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE=None), so the two live readings of how the gateway
charges actions DISAGREE IN SIGN:
  actions-to-level charge (this harness): score sum 9.06 -> 9.23 at b2000 (+1.9%)
  total-action charge (pessimistic):      0.243 -> 0.043 at b2000 (x0.18)
Matched per-cell, already-won games lose 6.2x at b1000, 25.2x at b2000, 100.5x at b4000
-- textbook quadratic. Enabling the early-stop grace removes the disagreement.

LLM-off by design and stated as such: every LLM-on row in the record is budget 400, so
the LLM-on crossing is reported as a BAND between two attributions, not a number.

Instrumentation census first: 0 None-valued diagnostics, observe channel alive on 400/400
cells, HUD flat fields readable on 400/400 (the 2dd60fce2 repair), all eight gated flags
pinned. Contention control: 12 matched cells against an uncontended serial run, 1.72x
wall inflation with outcomes IDENTICAL -- so the win curve is unaffected and the reported
times are conservative.

